  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nTuesday-Wednesday:\nAdditional weak shortwave energy translates through the mid-\nlevels into mid-week, though moisture return remains limited.\nSome guidance suggests a touch better saturation into the mid-\nlevels may support a few isolated showers or sprinkles on\nTuesday evening into Tuesday night, though confidence remains\nlow. Any activity would occur west of Highway 65, where 10-15%\nPoPs were introduced. Otherwise, the forecast remains rather\nquiet with most areas remaining dry. A gradual warming trend\ntowards the middle to upper 70s occurs on Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nThursday-Sunday:\nA ridge further amplifies into the later part of this week,\nsupporting high temperatures in the upper 70s to around 80. This\nis anywhere from the 5 to 10 degrees above normal for mid to\nlate October. Additionally, the trough and associated shortwave\nenergy become displaced further west of the area. Thus, any PoPs\nwill remain well west of the area through late this week and \nthis weekend. The signal for above normal temperatures (70-80% \nchance) persists into late October, as captured by the latest \nCPC 8 to 14 day outlook.",
